@vsm 1.2.1
@status archived
// docs/spec_revision/archive/examples/vsm_logic_demo.vsm — a WORKED EXAMPLE,
// ¬a specification of record.
// ARCHIVED 2026-08-17 (ARCHIVE-POLICY): la respuesta ya está dada (declaración,
// no razonamiento); DATED RECORD — citado por linage, ¬autoridad.
// It answers one question with running code instead of prose: can VSM
// structural logic be decided deterministically?
//
// The question came from rmw3 2026-08-09. The measured answer is that the
// REASONING was never the blocker. OWL 2 RL derives A1/A4/D6 violations 3/3
// with 0 false positives — over facts written BY HAND for the benchmark. Of
// 48 corpus documents, FOUR declare a V(...) a machine can read and ¬ONE
// declares its parent. A reasoner with ∄ facts decides nothing.
//
// So the blocker is a DECLARATION problem, and that is the same lesson this
// whole cycle produced from every other direction: `layer` was uncheckable
// while undeclared; @status drifted while one of its three senses had ∄ name.
// Structure inferred from prose is structure nobody can verify.

demo(VSM-LOGIC-DEMO-v1) {

  claim: "
    TIER 1 — STRUCTURAL — is decidable, and scripts/vsl/vsm_logic.py decides
    it: a finite graph with finite relations is first-order over a finite
    domain. A reasoner is a CONVENIENCE here, ¬a necessity.
    TIER 2 — QUANTITATIVE — is decidable GIVEN the numbers: A2 budget
    hierarchy, A8 absorption. Same blocker: the values must be declared.
    TIER 3 — SEMANTIC — is ¬decidable, and saying so is the point. Whether an
    axiom is TRUE, whether a compression lost what mattered, whether a claim's
    verifier is adequate. ≈70% of certification, done by READING."

  // ── The real topology, declared. VERIFIED against @state_db 2026-08-09:
  //    112 s1-clima RUNNING ▪ 113 s1-econ RUNNING ▪ 105 s1-bbh RUNNING.
  //    Declaring is DESIGN work and stays inside the S1 gate — ∄ container is
  //    touched, started, or wired by this document.
  // CORRECTED — and the correction is the demonstration. I first declared
  // the nucleus at level 0 from memory. The checker immediately reported
  // `D6 vsf-nucleus: S4 uses an LLM at level 0 — requires level ≥ 2`.
  // Investigating, the defect was in MY DECLARATION, ¬in the system: PH-12's
  // contracts (written by DS the same hour) state the nucleus at L=2, citing
  // kernel.rs. At L=2 an LLM in S4 is exactly what D6 permits.
  // This is the whole argument in one instance. A restated-from-memory level
  // inverted, a mechanical check caught it in under a second, and the correct
  // value was already declared somewhere a reader would have had to find.
  structure(V) = {
    id:      "vsf-nucleus"
    level:   2
    parent:  ∅
    s4_llm:  ⊤
  }

  structure(V) = {
    id:      "s1-clima"
    level:   3
    parent:  "vsf-nucleus"
    s4_llm:  ⊥
    couples: [ "s1-econ" via "vsf-nucleus".S3 ]
  }

  structure(V) = {
    id:      "s1-econ"
    level:   3
    parent:  "vsf-nucleus"
    s4_llm:  ⊥
  }

  decided: "
    A1  ∀ child: level = level(parent) + 1, relation one-way
    A4  ∀ coupling to a sibling: mediator named ∧ mediator = parent's S3
    D6  s4_llm = ⊤ ⟹ level ≥ 2
    S3* is a CHANNEL, ¬a tuple element — enforced by the SHAPE: the block has
        ∄ slot for it among subsystems, so it cannot be written as one.
        A constraint the notation makes unwritable needs ∄ checker."

  not_decided: "
    A2 budget ▪ A8 absorption ▪ Ω membership ▪ Lyapunov descent — Tier 2, and
    they need declared values, ¬declared structure.
    Everything in Tier 3. This file makes ∄ claim about it."

  // VSM-STRUCTURE-NOT-DECLARED — CLOSED. rmw3 (S5) approved structure(V)
  // on 2026-08-09 and it is declared in boot/vsl_language §grammar
  // (structure_def ::= …). The debt stayed open one day past its decision
  // because I registered the ratification in the GRAMMAR and never came back
  // to the marker that asked for it. A decision taken is ¬a debt closed until
  // the register says so — the register is the source of truth, ¬my memory of
  // having done it.
}

